collision detection:
	player enters their desired move (left, right, rotate, or nothing)
		transformation = (desired_y, desired_x, desired_shape)
			(desired y and x are ABSOLUTE not relative.)
		currentState = list of each block's coords.
		desiredState = list of each block's coords after transformation.
	FIRST detect collision with player's desired move ONLY.
	THEN detect collision with gravity.
		makes it so that even if player inputs an invalid move, piece can still
		 move down.
	detectCollision():
		loop through each position in desiredState:
			return 1 if ANY position is out of bounds
			return 1 if ANY position overlaps with board data.
			else: return 0
	if detectCollision(): keep currentState as it is.

game cycles through three states:
1. move tetromino
while q not pressed:
	generate next tetromino
	while new tetromino is in play (not locked):
		gameplay logic...
		if collision with ground --> lock tetromino.
	save tetromino to board data
	clear any lines in board data
	update score
